{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04A1", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:061e479679e93cdd41ff8ea894d0e88ec951e954c47b1df401a8a5b1159ac3f9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe only add this here so that we can later say that coarse quotients\ncorrespond to coarse moduli spaces (or moduli schemes).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:206a17be72f77fc5a197b420ce07a0828053c23769f052f97ff1840db8dd4612", "unit_id": "tag:04A1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04A1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$S = B$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "MATH_0012": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-coarse}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4435635741752cc3f6c6c4d21372a9f63e34ba4e03b8c8687d40390507d8898e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0bc3463ceb0eb5d1d0a5663c0773e869dfd7fd38907bf972e7f1640aaa7b00bd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and <MATH_0002> an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation.\nA morphism <MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nis called a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>coarse quotient<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0007> is a categorical quotient, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0008> is an orbit space.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIf <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>, <MATH_0011> are all schemes, then we say a morphism of schemes\n<MATH_0012> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>coarse quotient in schemes<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0013> is a categorical quotient in schemes, and\n<STRUCT_0007> <MATH_0014> is an orbit space.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3df8d06872cdbf60262ca100ca8f99af77f3fb5e929f7e870afa2c2bde2abc08", "unit_id": "tag:04A2:statement"}
